<title>UK: Brown briefing not on monetary policy-UK Treasury.</title>
<headline>Brown briefing not on monetary policy-UK Treasury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown's news briefing on Wednesday will not cover monetary policy, a Treasury spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Some gilt market traders had speculated the Chancellor might announce a new inflation target at the briefing, but the Treasury spokesman said details of the inflation target would be contained in the Mansion House speech on June 12.</p>
<p>The spokesman did not say what the briefing would cover.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
